  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CITES CoP17 coordination workshop between West and Central African countries and the United States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant will provide funding to Born Free USA to assist Senegal in facilitating the organization of a three day meeting between 20 West and Central African countries and the US Fish and Wildlife Service. Support provided to the West/Central African region for the organization of the meeting will include logistical assistance and support related to the development and translation of meeting documents including a draft enforcement declaration, draft listing proposals and draft working documents and any other document necessary to help build regional consensus. Discussion of meeting documents will be followed by discussions on the designation of specific issue leaders mandated by the region to take specific issues forward on the way up to and at CoP17. A section of the meeting will be devoted to building strategic alliances between the United States and countries in West and Central African countries on issues of common interest. The project team will also provide support to meeting participants designated as issue leaders on.specific issues after the meeting to assist with anything related to the submission of CoP17 documents. This project will be conducted as described in the Born Free USA grant proposal.</narrative>
  </description>
